f 17592186045417] [17592186053873 #edb/ref 1080 "3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186053873 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186053873 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f635c719-7dbf-57ed-934c-f9de54e7fa8d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186053874 #edb/ref 1080 "-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186053874 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186053874 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "04ecf807-8e84-5c03-a433-6bde37f36528" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186053875 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186053875 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186053875 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "50b0a37a-93ab-5fd9-802f-267f933ddfca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186053876 #edb/ref 1080 "-3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186053876 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186053876 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7060eba6-90f9-5e65-979e-0155bd147af6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054511 #edb/ref 1069 "e-2372" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054511 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the $x$-coordinate of the point $P$?\n\n![](images/cf/cf628679e0e9726a0db5d3399d992a0333911be16b8ccd89d2d6455e540ea3d9.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054511 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e4658959-f2fb-5bb4-ad05-d75b7c74a5d5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054511 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the coordinates of $P$, we start at the origin, move $3$ units *left*, and then $2$ units *up*.\n\n![](images/2d/2df77be5e817368e4082061f623ab2c10f2ec7f2ebd042864a1418e0aa67592f.png)\n\nThe coordinates of $P$ are $({\\color{red}{-3}},{\\color{blue}{2}})$. Therefore, the $x$-coordinate of $P$ is ${\\color{red}{-3}}$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054597 #edb/ref 1069 "e-974" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054597 #edb/ref 1071 "Plot the point $C$ with coordinates $(1,-2)$ on the Cartesian plane." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054597 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f610b8b9-8e9e-5a64-bc52-c1f939a0f147" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054597 #edb/ref 1074 "Starting at the origin $O$, we move along the $x$ and $y$ axes to get to the point $C$.\n\nFirst, we move along the $x$-axis. The point $C$ has an $x$-coordinate of $1$, so we move $1$ unit to the *right*, in the *positive* direction of the $x$-axis.\n\nThen, we move along the $y$-axis. The point $C$ has a $y$-coordinate of $-2$, so we move $2$ units *down*, in the *negative* direction of the $y$-axis.\n\n![](images/49/49069b4b9be29c0a999e7d2b71eec9a973eda9ad1f8a2a7b897d76970771a644.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054598 #edb/ref 1069 "e-975" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054598 #edb/ref 1071 "What are the $xy$-coordinates of the point $D$ shown below?\n\n![](images/c5/c546e2deb5b19c0068fd4ad550f97d3ee3143ec75bf96ca59ce5c44b825ab79e.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054598 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bda7aaff-f03f-53bd-b114-d28a46599641" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054598 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the coordinates of $D$, we inspect its position along the $x$ and $y$ axes.\n\nThe point $D$ is $3$ units to the *left* of the origin, in the *negative* direction of the $x$-axis. So, $D$ has an $x$-coordinate of $-3$.\n\nAdditionally, the point $D$ is $2$ units *below* the origin, in the *negative* direction of the $y$-axis. So, $D$ has a $y$-coordinate of $-2$.\n\nThe point $D$ has an $x$-coordinate of $-3$ and a $y$-coordinate of $-2$, so its coordinates are $(-3,-2)$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054599 #edb/ref 1069 "e-977" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054599 #edb/ref 1071 "To which quadrant does the point $(4,-2)$ belong?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054599 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "419738bb-56e5-52db-aa34-42ccd945fe64" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054599 #edb/ref 1074 "In order to identify the quadrant to which the point $(4,-2)$ belongs, we start by plotting the point.\n\n- The $x$-coordinate of the point is $4$, so we move $4$ units to the right of the origin.\n- The $y$-coordinate of the point is $-2$, so we move $2$ units down from the origin.\n\n![](images/02/02b0dd5d2d125277ffb6fc637fa612eef451c06522efa7655d8374c68641e796.png)\n\nBased on the graph, we can tell that the point belongs to quadrant $\\textrm{IV}$, the fourth quadrant." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054806 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049429 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054806 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049884 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054806 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050618 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054806 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186055434 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054806 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186055439 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054806 #edb/ref 1039 "Determining the X- or Y-Coordinate of a Point in the Coordinate Plane" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054806 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186054511 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054806 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "f41c2f3b-9b55-5f32-bb0a-a8397cdf66ce" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054807 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186055411 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054807 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186055435 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054807 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186235487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054807 #edb/ref 1039 "Identifying the Coordinates of a Point" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054807 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186054598 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054807 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "b509b42a-c38a-5400-8f93-f3e9024b16a2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054808 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049429 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054808 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049884 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054808 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050618 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054808 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186055120 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054808 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186055436 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054808 #edb/ref 1039 "Plotting a Point in the Coordinate Plane" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054808 #edb/ref 1041 #ed